{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789000615,"nonce":"5cOY67BEp9qEQeeRSrh04IibmXo=","message":"No longer reproduces after 33adae6. The panic was in lowering the WIDENED code, not narrow-integer arithmetic as this issue's title says -- refusing to widen a loop whose induction step cannot be rescaled removed the vector instructions Cranelift had no rule for.\n\nSame reproducer now runs --mode jit through to completion with no panic and no vector_size error.\n\nSo the title and the diagnosis here were both wrong: the trigger was a UI8 loop, but the shape Cranelift choked on was the widener's output. Closing as fixed by that commit, with the caveat that a Cranelift lowering gap for genuinely narrow scalar arithmetic -- if one exists -- is unproven either way, because this program no longer produces the IR that exposed it.\n\nWhat the same reproducer DID expose is a separate wrong answer under --mode jit, filed as 9c5e47e.","files":null}]}